    1-. "<div>1. Select an address space<br />and bank, then choose<br />Emulator default,<br />Little-endian or Big-endian</div><div style='font-size: 70%'></div>" .->24
    24-. "<div>2. Invoke the registered<br />scoped debugger and<br />presentation commands</div><div style='font-size: 70%'></div>" .->5
    5-. "<div>3. Capture the selected<br />instance, CPU, map revision<br />and display choice</div><div style='font-size: 70%'>[RelayCommand or AsyncRelayCommand]</div>" .->11
    11-. "<div>4. Send the registered view<br />request and captured context</div><div style='font-size: 70%'>[IView events]</div>" .->8
    8-. "<div>5. Dispatch the typed<br />inspection or preference<br />operation</div><div style='font-size: 70%'></div>" .->10
    10-. "<div>6. Recheck the selected scope<br />and resolve the effective<br />display order</div><div style='font-size: 70%'></div>" .->25
    25-. "<div>7. Save the display<br />preference for later debugger<br />views</div><div style='font-size: 70%'></div>" .->37
    10-. "<div>8. Issue a bounded read using<br />the selected space, bank and<br />map revision</div><div style='font-size: 70%'></div>" .->22
    22-. "<div>9. Publish the correlated raw<br />bytes with the actual map and<br />instance identity</div><div style='font-size: 70%'></div>" .->20
    25-. "<div>10. Project multibyte display<br />values using the effective<br />display order</div><div style='font-size: 70%'></div>" .->20
    11-. "<div>11. Read the current bytes,<br />rendered values and<br />applicable scope</div><div style='font-size: 70%'></div>" .->20
    24-. "<div>12. Render the memory map,<br />raw bytes and effective byte<br />order</div><div style='font-size: 70%'></div>" .->11

